# Fibonacci in lambda plus merge, with no label: scored points of the
# label-free family.
#
# THE PROGRAM is the naive recursion, fib(0) = 0, fib(1) = 1 and
# fib(n) = fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2), on a Scott unary n with a binary
# result, its addition the binary plus of contest_merge_dynamic.pl, let
# bound once. The test compares fib(n) with a claimed binary numeral.
#
# THE QUESTION IT ASKS (2026-09-28): the labeled family
# (contest_inheritance_fibonacci.pl) costs about 1.7 a step because its two
# recursive calls spell n - 2 differently. Here n - 1 and n - 2 are
# subterms of the one numeral n, so the calls are spelled the same, and a
# reading that tables by spelling shares them.
#
# THE REFERENCE (reference_fibonacci/2) is the iteration, n additions of
# numbers of O(n) bits, O(n^2): a doubling of n costs 4.
#
# READINGS (2026-09-28, CPU 3 under contest_limited.sh, a fresh process per
# reading, the boolean(true) template, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB):
# - weak_head: fib(10), fib(15) and fib(20) in 51, 491 and 5795 ms, about
#   1.6 a step, exponential as the labeled family;
# - tabling(weak_head): fib(20), 40, 80 and 160 in 50, 156, 599 and 3052
#   ms, a doubling costing 3.1, 3.8 and 5.1 against the reference's 4;
#   fib(320) stopped (7188 ms). The answer to the question: without labels,
#   tabling shares the two calls, and the growth is polynomial;
# - records_routed(record_interned(tabling(weak_head)), weak_head): fib(20)
#   in 5759 ms and fib(40) stopped. A label-free program has no record,
#   so the record reading reads it as weak_head does.
# The sizes are 20, 40 and 80 (n, 2n and 4n), 160 at the edge and 320
# beyond, and a wrong claim at 40, fib(40) = 102334155 with bit 25 flipped,
# which the comparison reaches only after the 25 bits below it.
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - the iteration of the reference, reached from the recursive definition by
#   remembering each fib(k) once: D. Michie, "Memo" Functions and Machine
#   Learning, Nature 1968, doi:10.1038/218019a0.
# - tabled evaluation: W. Chen, D. S. Warren, Tabled Evaluation with
#   Delaying for General Logic Programs, J. ACM 1996,
#   doi:10.1145/227595.227597.

#   fibonacci_point(?Point, ?N, ?Claimed)
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. export
